# build-ffmpeg-macos.sh is written on Windows and executed on macOS. A checkout made with
# core.autocrlf=false would otherwise commit CRLF, and bash reports that as
# `$'\r': command not found` on the second line — a failure that names neither the file nor the
# cause. Pinning eol=lf here costs nothing and removes the possibility.
*.sh text eol=lf
